{{ElectionsMD}}
The '''2018 United States House of Representatives elections in Maryland''' will be held on November 6, 2018, electing the eight [[United States House of Representatives|U.S. Representatives]] from the [[Maryland|State of Maryland]], one from each of the state's eight [[Maryland's congressional districts|congressional districts]]. The elections will coincide with the [[Maryland gubernatorial election, 2018|gubernatorial election]], as well as [[United States House of Representatives elections, 2018|other elections]] to the House of Representatives, [[United States Senate elections, 2018|elections]] to the [[United States Senate]] and various [[United States elections, 2018#State elections|state]] and [[United States elections, 2018#Local elections|local elections]].

{{Toclimit|limit=2}}
==District 1==
{{see also|Maryland's 1st congressional district}}
The incumbent is Republican [[Andy Harris (politician)|Andy Harris]], who has represented the district since 2011. Harris was re-elected with 67% of the vote in 2016.

The [[Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee]] included Maryland's 1st congressional district on its initial list of Republican-held seats considered targets in 2018.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.politico.com/story/2017/01/dccc-2018-targets-234366|title=Amid Democratic doldrums, DCCC identifies 2018 targets|work=[[Politico]]|last=Cheney|first=Kyle|date=January 30, 2017|accessdate=February 11, 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://action.dccc.org/pdf/dccc-on-offense.pdf|title=House Democrats Playing Offense|work=[[Democratic Congressional Campaign Committee]]|last=Sena|first=Dan|date=January 30, 2017|accessdate=February 11, 2017}}</ref>

